<section class="section" id="faq">
  <h2>Massage FAQs</h2>
  <div class="faq-list">
    <details class="faq-item" open>
      <summary>What are your prices and session lengths?</summary>
      <div class="faq-body">
        <p>90 minutes is $150<br>75 minutes is $135<br>50 minutes is $100</p>
      </div>
    </details>
    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>How do I know how long of a session to book?</summary>
      <div class="faq-body">
        <p><strong>90 minutes</strong> — This is my bread-and-butter length. 90 minutes bakes in time for a full body massage with some time to address specific problems, and ensure the nervous system has time to sink into relaxation and recovery. I highly suggest this for first-time clients to ensure there's enough time to explore and get to know what's going on in your body to create a comprehensive plan moving forward.</p>
        <p><strong>75 minutes</strong> — Great if you want a quick full body massage, without extra time for any specific work in problem areas. This is great if you are not working with a specific issue, but working on general recovery and well-being.</p>
        <p><strong>50 minutes*</strong> — Great if you have a specific problem we're working on addressing, like a shoulder, hip, or back problem. This is generally a maintenance appointment. *50-minute sessions are only offered for established clients.</p>
      </div>
    </details>
    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Do you do deep tissue massage?</summary>
      <div class="faq-body">
        <p><strong>Yes, and…</strong> deep tissue massage is less about how much pressure is applied, and more about how willingly the tissue relaxes to allow deeper work. This means to get "deep tissue massage" I may employ deep pressure, cupping, scraping, nervous system relaxation, or a combo of techniques to make sure your body is receiving the work it needs to work at its optimal level.</p>
      </div>
    </details>
    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Do you take insurance?</summary>
      <div class="faq-body">
        <p>At this time, I do not accept insurance. If you would like to submit a receipt with notes for reimbursement, please inform me before our session so I can make sure patient notes are properly documented.</p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>
